From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Butterworth <i.r.butterworth@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:38:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] inference: Keep source for output only without native code on
 1.13

The backport of #64210 keeps the source of every compileable method while
generating output. A kept source can call another method through a bare
`MethodInstance`, which 1.13's native code collection does not follow, so
`--trim` failed to compile such callees and the trimming test failed trim
verification. Master follows these edges under `--trim` since #62001.

Keep the source only when the output has no native code, which is the
`.ji` cache case #64210 is for.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Claude Opus 5.5)
---
 Compiler/src/typeinfer.jl | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Compiler/src/typeinfer.jl b/Compiler/src/typeinfer.jl
index f6d15c8a8eea38857a742bf04c83c730da2e0e17..1171b1830b36e6c20d05c0a3ce2c7e387fac6ba0 100644
--- a/Compiler/src/typeinfer.jl
+++ b/Compiler/src/typeinfer.jl
@@ -444,7 +444,7 @@ end
 # A cache without native code needs the source of every compileable signature, or
 # loading it means inferring them all again. Caches with native code drop it on save.
 keep_source_for_output(mi::MethodInstance) =
-    ccall(:jl_generating_output, Cint, ()) != 0 && isa_compileable_sig(mi)
+    ccall(:jl_generating_output, Cint, ()) != 0 && JLOptions().outputo == C_NULL && isa_compileable_sig(mi)
 
 function maybe_compress_codeinfo(interp::AbstractInterpreter, mi::MethodInstance, ci::CodeInfo)
     def = mi.def
